      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "International organizations often encounter friction with national sovereignty due to their reliance on member state cooperation and voluntary compliance. Member states frequently prioritize their immediate political or economic interests over the broad mandates of the global body. Furthermore, the diffused authority and bureaucratic consensus-building process within these organizations often lead to watered-down resolutions that cannot effectively challenge deeply entrenched national prerogatives.",
